WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.256
Emperor Wu of Liang, Xiao Yan, was a deeply devout Buddhist.

00:00:05.606 --> 00:00:10.766
Every day he chanted sutras and worshipped the Buddha, devout at heart.

00:00:11.116 --> 00:00:14.716
He built many temples and supported Buddhist learning everywhere.

00:00:15.066 --> 00:00:21.450
One day, he suddenly decided to set down the throne and enter a temple to become a monk.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:27.272
He changed into monk's robes, moved into the temple, and lived together with the monks.

00:00:27.622 --> 00:00:33.190
All at once the palace had no emperor, and the officials were frantic with worry.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:37.572
They discussed it back and forth, but could think of no other good solution.

00:00:37.922 --> 00:00:43.922
With no other way, everyone pooled a great deal of gold, silver and treasure to ransom the emperor back.

00:00:44.272 --> 00:00:49.096
Only then was the emperor fully satisfied, and he returned to the palace to go on being emperor.

00:00:49.446 --> 00:00:54.126
Such a thing actually happened several times — it truly left people not knowing whether to laugh or cry.

00:00:54.476 --> 00:00:59.420
Faith is a good thing in itself, but nothing should be taken too far.

